---

<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="50–60 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Technology &amp; devices: <em>report what you can observe</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Useful technology English identifies the device or service, the action attempted, the observable symptom, and the scope of the problem. It asks for a safe next step without guessing a technical cause or exposing private account information.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">50–60 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">device · action · symptom · scope</span>
    <span class="tag">download · install · restart · reset</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Find six information jobs in one support request.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Separate hardware, software, connection, account, and file language.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose exact actions, symptoms, scope, and safe responses.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Give a fictional support report without private data.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can distinguish a device from an app, account, network, and file; distinguish downloading from installing, uploading, saving, and backing up; place pronouns accurately in common technology phrasal verbs; report what will not open, load, connect, charge, or play; state when and where a problem occurs; ask for a safe next step; and refuse requests for passwords or verification codes.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved an action happening now, a polite imperative, and a present-perfect result relevant now.">
    <h3>Three earlier patterns</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use present continuous for the action now, a base-verb imperative for the instruction, and present perfect for the completed save with a result now.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier pattern choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is downloading">is downloading</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Download">Download</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has saved">has saved</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="downloads">downloads</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Downloads">Downloads</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="saved">saved</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The progress bar is moving right now: The laptop <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is downloading" data-hint="Use is plus verb-ing for the download in progress now." data-fix="The laptop is downloading the update right now." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the update right now.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The support note gives a direct instruction with no subject: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Download" data-hint="Begin an affirmative imperative with the base verb Download." data-fix="Download the file from the official course page." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the file from the official course page.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The save is complete, so the document is protected before restart: Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has saved" data-hint="Use has plus the past participle because the completed save has a result now." data-fix="Maya has saved the document, so it is safe to restart the app." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the document, so it is safe to restart the app.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice six jobs in one support request</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Harbor Learning support message</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“I’m using <strong>a shared Windows laptop</strong> in the training room. I <strong>opened the Harbor Learning website and selected Upload</strong>, but <strong>the progress bar stays at 0 percent</strong>. The problem started <strong>at 10:15</strong>. Other websites open on this laptop, and <strong>the same file uploads from the office tablet</strong>. The page says <strong>‘Upload failed. Try again.’</strong> What should I try next?”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which phrase identifies the device and location? Which phrase reports the attempted action?</li>
      <li>Which parts report the symptom, time, scope, and exact message?</li>
      <li>Does the writer diagnose the cause, or ask for a next step?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You identified the device and location, attempted action, observable symptom, time, scope check, and exact message.">
    <h3>Discovery check: identify each information job</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Support information choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="device and location">device and location</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="attempted action">attempted action</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="observable symptom">observable symptom</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="start time">start time</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="scope check">scope check</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="exact message">exact message</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">A shared Windows laptop in the training room</span> gives the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="device and location" data-hint="The phrase names both the hardware and where the writer is using it." data-fix="A shared Windows laptop in the training room gives the device and location." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="ex">Opened the website and selected Upload</span> gives the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="attempted action" data-hint="These verbs report exactly what the writer did before the problem appeared." data-fix="Opening the site and selecting Upload give the attempted action." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="ex">The progress bar stays at 0 percent</span> gives the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="observable symptom" data-hint="The writer reports a visible result instead of guessing why it happens." data-fix="A progress bar that stays at 0 percent is the observable symptom." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">At 10:15</span> gives the problem’s <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="start time" data-hint="This clock point states when the problem began." data-fix="At 10:15 is the start time." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The facts that other sites open and the file uploads from another device provide a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="scope check" data-hint="These comparisons show what is and is not affected." data-fix="The other-site and other-device comparisons provide the scope check." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><span class="ex">Upload failed. Try again.</span> gives the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="exact message" data-hint="The writer copies the visible words without including private credentials." data-fix="Upload failed. Try again. is the exact message." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: name the technology layer</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">My computer is broken</span> is often too broad. First identify which layer has the visible problem.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>layer</th><th>useful nouns</th><th>example report</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>hardware device or part</td><td><span class="ex">laptop, phone, screen, keyboard, charger, headphones</span></td><td><span class="ex">The keyboard does not respond.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>app or software</td><td><span class="ex">app, browser, program, update</span></td><td><span class="ex">The video app will not open.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>connection or network</td><td><span class="ex">Wi-Fi network, mobile data, Bluetooth connection</span></td><td><span class="ex">The laptop cannot connect to this Wi-Fi network.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>account or access</td><td><span class="ex">account, username, password, verification code</span></td><td><span class="ex">I can open the site, but I cannot log in to my account.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>file or location</td><td><span class="ex">file, document, photo, folder, link, page</span></td><td><span class="ex">The file is in Downloads, but it will not open.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Report the symptom before diagnosing the cause. <span class="ex">The page will not load</span> is observable. <span class="ex">The router is broken</span> is a diagnosis that may be wrong. A helper can ask about other pages, devices, networks, times, or accounts to narrow the scope.</p>

  <h2>Keep the action and result distinct</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>action</th><th>meaning</th><th>different action</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">download a file</span></td><td>transfer it from an online location to this device</td><td><span class="ex">upload a file</span> transfers it from this device to an online location</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">download an app</span></td><td>receive its installation file or package</td><td><span class="ex">install the app</span> makes the software ready to use</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">save the document</span></td><td>store the current changes</td><td><span class="ex">back up the document</span> keeps a separate recovery copy</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">restart the device</span></td><td>shut it down and start it again</td><td><span class="ex">reset the device</span> changes settings and may erase information</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">connect to Wi-Fi</span></td><td>join a network</td><td><span class="ex">pair the headphones</span> creates a Bluetooth relationship between devices</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">mute the microphone</span></td><td>stop its sound from being sent</td><td><span class="ex">turn off the microphone</span> may disable the device or feature completely</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">Restart</span> and <span class="ex">reset</span> are not synonyms. Save work first, then restart only when the device, app, official support, or workplace policy permits it. Do not reset a device merely because a restart was suggested.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished download, upload, install, back up, restart, and pair from their nearby but different actions.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the exact action</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Technology action choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="download">download</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="upload">upload</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="install">install</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="back up">back up</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="restart">restart</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="pair">pair</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The report is on the official course site, and Maya needs a copy on her laptop: She should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="download" data-hint="Download transfers the file from the online course site to Maya’s device." data-fix="Maya should download the report from the official course site." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the report.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Leo has a photo on his phone and needs to add it to the class portal: He should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="upload" data-hint="Upload transfers the file from Leo’s device to the online portal." data-fix="Leo should upload the photo to the class portal." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the photo.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The app package is already on the laptop, but the app is not ready to open: Maya still needs to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="install" data-hint="Install makes downloaded software ready to use." data-fix="Maya still needs to install the app." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the app.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Before changing the laptop, Leo needs a separate recovery copy of the project folder: He should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="back up" data-hint="Back up means create a separate recovery copy, not merely save current changes." data-fix="Leo should back up the project folder before the change." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the project folder.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Official support says to shut down and start the laptop again without changing its settings: Maya should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="restart" data-hint="Restart turns the device off and on again without requesting a settings reset." data-fix="Maya should save her work and restart the laptop." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the laptop after saving her work.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The new Bluetooth headphones and phone have never been connected to each other: Leo needs to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="pair" data-hint="Pair creates the first Bluetooth relationship between the two devices." data-fix="Leo needs to pair the Bluetooth headphones with his phone." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the headphones with his phone.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Place the object inside the correct chunk</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Some phrasal verbs are separable. A noun can follow the whole chunk or sit in the middle: <span class="ex">turn on the laptop</span> or <span class="ex">turn the laptop on</span>. A pronoun must sit in the middle: <span class="ex">turn it on</span>, not <span class="ex">turn on it</span>.</p>
  <p>Other combinations keep their preposition with the following noun: <span class="ex">log in to your account, connect to the network, search for the file</span>. Do not apply the pronoun rule from <span class="ex">turn it on</span> to every verb with a small word.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>structure</th><th>natural example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>separable verb + noun</td><td><span class="ex">plug in the charger · plug the charger in</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>separable verb + pronoun</td><td><span class="ex">plug it in · turn it off</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>verb + fixed preposition + noun</td><td><span class="ex">log in to the portal · connect to Wi-Fi · search for the document</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>send + person + thing</td><td><span class="ex">send me the link</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>send + thing + to + person</td><td><span class="ex">send the link to me</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You placed pronouns inside separable verbs and preserved the fixed prepositions in account, network, search, and send patterns.">
    <h3>Drill 2: complete the whole chunk</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Technology structure choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="turn it on">turn it on</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="plug it in">plug it in</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="log in to">log in to</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="connect to">connect to</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="search for">search for</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="send me">send me</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The laptop is off, and <span class="ex">it</span> replaces <span class="ex">the laptop</span>: Please <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="turn it on" data-hint="Put the pronoun it between turn and on." data-fix="Please turn it on." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The normal, undamaged charger is beside the laptop, and <span class="ex">it</span> replaces <span class="ex">the charger</span>: Please <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="plug it in" data-hint="Put the pronoun it between plug and in." data-fix="Please plug it in using the correct outlet and charger." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Maya wants to enter the official course account: She needs to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="log in to" data-hint="Keep in to together before the account destination." data-fix="She needs to log in to the official course account." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the official course account.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The laptop needs to join the named Harbor Guest network: It needs to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="connect to" data-hint="Connect to introduces the network being joined." data-fix="It needs to connect to the Harbor Guest network." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the Harbor Guest network.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Leo cannot find the document in the folder: He should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="search for" data-hint="Search for introduces the item Leo is trying to find." data-fix="He should search for the document by its exact filename." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the document by its exact filename.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The speaker wants the link, with the person directly after <span class="ex">send</span>: Could you <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="send me" data-hint="Use send plus person plus thing: send me the official link." data-fix="Could you send me the official link?" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the official link?</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Report the symptom and scope before the solution</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>observable symptom</th><th>useful scope or time detail</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">The laptop will not turn on.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The charging light is also off.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">The screen is frozen.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The pointer has not moved for two minutes.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">The page will not load.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Other pages load on the same device.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">There is no sound in the call.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Music plays normally in another app.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">The battery is not charging.</span></td><td><span class="ex">It has stayed at 12 percent for twenty minutes.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">I cannot log in.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The page says “Password incorrect,” but I will not share my password.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>In problem reports, <span class="ex">will not</span> or <span class="ex">won’t</span> can mean that a device or app fails or refuses to perform an action: <span class="ex">The app won’t open.</span> It is not a prediction here.</p>
  <p>A useful request is <span class="ex">What should I try next?</span> or <span class="ex">Is it safe to restart the app?</span> A helper can answer with one limited step and a check: <span class="ex">Save the document first. Then close and reopen the app. Tell me whether the same message appears.</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You selected six observable symptoms with enough device, app, scope, time, or message context for one defensible report.">
    <h3>Drill 3: choose the precise symptom</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Technology symptom choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will not turn on">will not turn on</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is frozen">is frozen</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will not load">will not load</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has no sound">has no sound</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is not charging">is not charging</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cannot log in">cannot log in</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Maya presses the laptop’s power button, but no light or image appears: The laptop <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will not turn on" data-hint="Report the failed power action without diagnosing the battery or charger." data-fix="The laptop will not turn on, and no light appears." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The image remains visible, but the pointer and keyboard have not responded for two minutes: The screen <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is frozen" data-hint="Frozen describes a visible display that remains stuck and does not respond." data-fix="The screen is frozen; the pointer and keyboard have not responded for two minutes." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The course page stays blank, although two other pages open on the same laptop: The course page <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will not load" data-hint="Will not load reports the blank page while the comparison limits the scope." data-fix="The course page will not load, but other pages open on the same laptop." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Maya hears music in another app, but she hears nothing in the video call: The video call <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has no sound" data-hint="Has no sound reports the call symptom while the music comparison narrows the scope." data-fix="The video call has no sound, but music plays in another app." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The normal-looking phone and correct charger have been connected for twenty minutes, but the battery remains at 12 percent: The battery <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is not charging" data-hint="Report the unchanged percentage rather than guessing which part is broken." data-fix="The battery is not charging; it has stayed at 12 percent for twenty minutes." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The official portal opens, but after Maya enters her username the page says <span class="ex">Password incorrect</span>: Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="cannot log in" data-hint="Cannot log in reports the access result without exposing the actual password." data-fix="Maya cannot log in; the official page says Password incorrect." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Safety boundary: protect the device and the account</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not share a real password, PIN, or verification code in a lesson, support chat, screenshot, or exercise. The U.S. Federal Trade Commission says a verification code is for your own login and should not be given to someone else. Use an official app, site, or trusted contact method for support. <a href="https://consumer.ftc.gov/consumer-alerts/2024/03/whats-verification-code-why-would-someone-ask-me-it">FTC verification-code guidance</a>.</li>
      <li>Do not open an unexpected link or attachment just because a message says it is urgent. Verify the sender through a known channel and follow your organization’s reporting process. <a href="https://www.cisa.gov/secure-our-world">CISA Secure Our World guidance</a>.</li>
      <li>If a battery becomes unusually hot, changes shape or color, leaks, smells strange, or makes odd noises, stop using and charging the device. Move away and follow the manufacturer’s, workplace’s, or local emergency guidance. Do not attempt a battery repair. <a href="https://www.usfa.fema.gov/prevention/home-fires/prevent-fires/batteries/">U.S. Fire Administration battery guidance</a>.</li>
      <li>Do not reset a device, erase data, install unknown software, or change security settings unless the owner or authorized support process clearly permits that action.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: stress the failed action and link the command</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Wi-Fi</span> is /ˈwaɪfaɪ/, <span class="ex">device</span> is /dɪˈvaɪs/, <span class="ex">password</span> is /ˈpæsˌwɝd/, and <span class="ex">error</span> is /ˈɛrɚ/ in common U.S. speech.</p>
    <p>Stress the action or symptom that carries the new information: <span class="ex">The page won’t <strong>LOAD</strong>. The battery isn’t <strong>CHARGING</strong>. The screen is <strong>FROZEN</strong>.</span> Keep <span class="ex">won’t /woʊnt/</span> distinct from <span class="ex">want /wɑnt/</span>.</p>
    <p>In separable commands, keep the pronoun light and stress the result: <span class="ex">turn it <strong>ON</strong> · plug it <strong>IN</strong> · back it <strong>UP</strong></span>. In connected U.S. speech, <span class="ex">Can you send me the link?</span> may begin /kənjə/, and <span class="ex">Could you restart the app?</span> may begin /kʊdʒə/.</p>
    <p>Chunk a support report by information job: <span class="ex">I’m using a shared laptop | the course page won’t load | other pages open normally | and the message says “Connection timed out.”</span></p>
  </div>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read device, attempted action, symptom, scope, exact message, and safe account response listening check">
    <h2>Listen for the support evidence</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p class="note-line"><b>Tutor-read listening:</b> Keep the transcript closed. Read each item once naturally and once after the learner chooses. Do not ask the learner to repeat or reveal real account information.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard the device, attempted action, observable symptom, limited scope, exact message, and safe refusal to share a verification code.">
      <h3>Six support-message decisions</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a shared Windows laptop" data-hint="Listen for the hardware and operating-system description after I’m using." data-fix="The speaker is using a shared Windows laptop."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which device is affected?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a shared Windows laptop">a shared Windows laptop</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a personal Android phone">a personal Android phone</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an office printer">an office printer</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The speaker selected Upload." data-hint="Listen for the action immediately before the progress problem." data-fix="The speaker selected Upload after opening the official page."><p class="quiz-question">2. What action did the speaker attempt?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker selected Upload.">The speaker selected Upload.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker reset the laptop.">The speaker reset the laptop.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker deleted the file.">The speaker deleted the file.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The progress bar stays at 0 percent." data-hint="Listen for the visible result after the action." data-fix="The progress bar stays at 0 percent."><p class="quiz-question">3. What observable symptom does the speaker report?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The progress bar stays at 0 percent.">The progress bar stays at 0 percent.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The battery is unusually hot.">The battery is unusually hot.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The screen has changed color.">The screen has changed color.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Other websites open on the laptop." data-hint="Listen for the comparison showing that the whole internet connection is not necessarily unavailable." data-fix="Other websites open on the same laptop."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which fact limits the problem’s scope?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Other websites open on the laptop.">Other websites open on the laptop.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="No device in the building has power.">No device in the building has power.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every app on every device is frozen.">Every app on every device is frozen.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Upload failed. Try again." data-hint="Listen for the exact words the page displays." data-fix="The exact message is Upload failed. Try again."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which exact message appears?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Upload failed. Try again.">Upload failed. Try again.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Password incorrect.">Password incorrect.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Battery critically low.">Battery critically low.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The speaker refuses and contacts support through the official app." data-hint="Listen for the safe response to an unexpected request for a private code." data-fix="The speaker refuses to share the code and contacts support through the official app."><p class="quiz-question">6. What does the speaker do when an unexpected caller asks for a verification code?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker refuses and contacts support through the official app.">The speaker refuses and contacts support through the official app.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker reads the verification code aloud.">The speaker reads the verification code aloud.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The speaker posts the code in a public chat.">The speaker posts the code in a public chat.</button></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>Tutor transcript and evidence notes</summary>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="ex">I’m using a shared Windows laptop in the training room.</span> Evidence target: device and location.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">I opened the official page and selected Upload.</span> Evidence target: attempted action.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">The progress bar stays at zero percent.</span> Evidence target: observable symptom.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">Other websites open on this laptop, and the file uploads from the office tablet.</span> Evidence target: scope.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">The exact message is “Upload failed. Try again.”</span> Evidence target: copied message without credentials.</li>
        <li><span class="ex">I won’t share my verification code. I’ll contact support through the official app.</span> Evidence target: safe account response.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </section>

  <h2>Read one complete support ticket</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Harbor Learning ticket 204</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">At 9:10, I tried to open the Harbor Learning portal on the shared training laptop. The page will not load, but two other websites open on the same laptop. The portal also opens on the office tablet using the same Wi-Fi network. I closed and reopened the browser, then typed the official address again. The message still says “Connection timed out.” I did not click the unexpected “support” link in a text message, and I did not share my password or verification code. What should I try next?</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the affected layer, scope comparison, attempted steps, and safe security response from the support ticket.">
    <h3>Reading check: use only ticket 204</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the Harbor Learning portal on the shared laptop" data-hint="The first sentence names both the affected service and device." data-fix="The affected service is the Harbor Learning portal on the shared training laptop."><p class="quiz-question">1. What is affected?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the Harbor Learning portal on the shared laptop">the Harbor Learning portal on the shared laptop</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="every website on every device">every website on every device</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the office tablet’s battery">the office tablet’s battery</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Other websites open, and the portal opens on the tablet." data-hint="The second and third sentences compare another site and another device." data-fix="Other websites open on the laptop, and the portal opens on the tablet."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which evidence limits the scope?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Other websites open, and the portal opens on the tablet.">Other websites open, and the portal opens on the tablet.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The whole building has no internet access.">The whole building has no internet access.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Every browser displays the same message.">Every browser displays the same message.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The writer reopened the browser and retyped the official address." data-hint="The fourth sentence lists the two steps already attempted." data-fix="The writer reopened the browser and retyped the official address."><p class="quiz-question">3. What has the writer already tried?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The writer reopened the browser and retyped the official address.">The writer reopened the browser and retyped the official address.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The writer reset and erased the laptop.">The writer reset and erased the laptop.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The writer installed software from the text message.">The writer installed software from the text message.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The writer avoided the unexpected link and kept credentials private." data-hint="The final statement names both the suspicious link and the private information not shared." data-fix="The writer avoided the unexpected link and kept the password and verification code private."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which safe action does the ticket report?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The writer avoided the unexpected link and kept credentials private.">The writer avoided the unexpected link and kept credentials private.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The writer sent the verification code to the caller.">The writer sent the verification code to the caller.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The writer opened and installed the unexpected attachment.">The writer opened and installed the unexpected attachment.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build a report and an action distinction</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the app will not open but other apps work" data-hint="Name the affected app and failed action first, then add the comparison that limits the scope." data-fix="The app will not open, but other apps work." data-success-message="Correct. The sentence reports an observable symptom and limits the scope with a comparison.">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the symptom and scope</h3><p class="tile-target">One app fails to open. Other apps on the same device work.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="other">other</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="open">open</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="app">app</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="will">will</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="apps">apps</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="but">but</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="work">work</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="not">not</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i downloaded the app but i have not installed it" data-hint="Report the completed transfer first, then use have not plus installed for the unfinished setup." data-fix="I downloaded the app, but I have not installed it." data-success-message="Correct. Downloaded reports the transfer; have not installed reports that setup is still incomplete.">
    <h3>Drill 5: build two different actions</h3><p class="tile-target">The app package is on the device, but the software is not ready to use.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="it">it</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="installed">installed</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="app">app</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="downloaded">downloaded</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="have">have</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="but">but</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="not">not</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair unsafe or imprecise instructions</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="on it" data-hint="The pronoun must sit between turn and on." data-fix="Please turn it on." data-why="Turn on is separable. With the pronoun it, place the object in the middle: turn it on." data-success-message="Correct. The pronoun belongs inside the separable chunk turn it on.">
    <h3>Drill 6: repair pronoun placement</h3><p>Tap the part that places the pronoun after the particle.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="please">Please</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="turn">turn</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="on it">on it.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="reset" data-hint="Official support requested an off-and-on cycle, not a settings change or erasure." data-fix="After saving the document, Maya restarted the laptop." data-why="Restart shuts down and starts again. Reset changes settings and may erase information, so it is not a synonym for restart." data-success-message="Correct. The requested off-and-on action is restart, not reset.">
    <h3>Drill 7: repair the action</h3><p>Support said, “Save your document, then shut down and start the laptop again.” Tap the word that reports a different action.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="after-saving">After saving</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the-document">the document,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="maya">Maya</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="reset">reset</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the-laptop">the laptop.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="verification code" data-hint="A private one-time code is only for the account owner’s own login." data-fix="I will not share my verification code. I will contact support through the official app." data-why="An unexpected support caller should not receive a password or verification code. End the contact and use a known official support channel." data-success-message="Correct. Verification codes stay private; use an official support channel instead.">
    <h3>Drill 8: reject the unsafe request</h3><p>An unexpected caller says, “I’m support.” Tap the private information in the caller’s request.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="please-send">Please send</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="me">me</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="your">your</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="verification code">verification code.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it without exposing private technology data</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real devices, employer, school, network name, email, username, password, PIN, verification code, files, messages, contacts, location, or account history. Use the fictional Harbor system. Real details are optional.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Fictional support card:</b> Shared Harbor laptop; official training portal; upload selected at 10:15; progress stays at 0 percent; other sites work; same file uploads from office tablet; exact message: <span class="ex">Upload failed. Try again.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Build the report:</b> Give the device and location, attempted action, observable symptom, time, two scope facts, exact message, and one safe request. Do not guess which technical part is broken.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Support response:</b> Ask whether the file is saved, give one authorized low-risk step, and ask what changes. Do not request credentials, install unknown software, reset the device, or invent a guaranteed fix.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Security interruption:</b> A message says, <span class="ex">“Urgent! Send your verification code now.”</span> Refuse, explain what stays private, and name the official channel you will use instead.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: give a 45–60 second fictional support report</h3>
    <p>Use the Harbor card or invent another fictional low-risk problem. Include the device or service, attempted action, observable symptom, start time, two scope checks, exact message, and a request for the next safe step. Then respond to one suspicious request without revealing private information.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener identify what works, what fails, what was already tried, and what remains unknown? Does every instruction stay within the fictional owner’s authorization?</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You protected action-result meaning, precise symptom reporting, authorized restart language, and private credentials.">
    <h3>Final check: choose the precise and safe response</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The course page will not load, but other pages open on this laptop." data-hint="Report the observable failure and the comparison without diagnosing the network." data-fix="The course page will not load, but other pages open on this laptop."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which report gives a precise symptom and scope without guessing the cause?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The course page will not load, but other pages open on this laptop.">The course page will not load, but other pages open on this laptop.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The entire internet is broken everywhere.">The entire internet is broken everywhere.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="This computer is bad.">This computer is bad.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Save the document, then restart the app if official support permits it." data-hint="Protect the work, use restart rather than reset, and keep the authorization condition." data-fix="Save the document, then restart the app if official support permits it."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which instruction protects work and stays inside authorization?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Save the document, then restart the app if official support permits it.">Save the document, then restart the app if official support permits it.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Reset and erase the laptop immediately.">Reset and erase the laptop immediately.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Install any program an unknown caller sends.">Install any program an unknown caller sends.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I downloaded the app, but I have not installed it." data-hint="The transfer is complete, but the software setup is not." data-fix="I downloaded the app, but I have not installed it."><p class="quiz-question">3. The app package is on the device, but the app is not ready to use. Which report is accurate?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I downloaded the app, but I have not installed it.">I downloaded the app, but I have not installed it.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I installed the app, but it has not downloaded.">I installed the app, but it has not downloaded.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I uploaded the app into my keyboard.">I uploaded the app into my keyboard.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="I will not share the code. I will contact support through the official app." data-hint="Keep the verification code private and independently use a known channel." data-fix="I will not share the code. I will contact support through the official app."><p class="quiz-question">4. An unexpected caller requests your verification code. Which response is safe?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I will not share the code. I will contact support through the official app.">I will not share the code. I will contact support through the official app.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I will read the code and my password aloud.">I will read the code and my password aloud.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I will post the code so everyone can help.">I will post the code so everyone can help.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect: observation or diagnosis?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the support system</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">Download moves...</span> <span class="ex">Upload moves...</span> <span class="ex">Install makes...</span> <span class="ex">Restart differs from reset because...</span> <span class="ex">A useful scope check compares...</span></p>
    <p>Then find one diagnosis in your own report and replace it with a visible symptom, time, message, or comparison. State one piece of information that must remain private.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the three-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
  </div>

